>> title: Aioli
>> category: Dressings & Dips
>> tags: garlic, eggs, olive oil, emulsion, no-cook
>> counters: Deli, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: garlic aioli, allioli, ali-oli, garlic mayonnaise
>> servings: 8
>> time: 20 min
>> slack: unforgiving — the same emulsion as mayonnaise with garlic pounded under it, and it breaks the same way: too much oil too fast and it splits into a slick that no amount of whisking gathers back up. It has to be rescued into a new yolk or thrown away
>> step.1: pound to a paste
>> step.2: whisk in
>> step.3: drizzle in drop by drop
>> step.4: loosen

Pound @garlic{4%cloves} with @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} to a smooth paste in a #mortar{}.

Whisk @egg yolk{1%large}(at room temperature) and @lemon juice{2%tsp} into @&(~1)garlic paste{}.

Drizzle @extra-virgin olive oil{3/4%cup}(180 mL) and @neutral oil{1/4%cup}(60 mL; keeps it from turning bitter) into @&(~1)base{} drop by drop at first, whisking until stiff.

Loosen @&(~1)aioli{} with @warm water{2%tsp} to a spoonable gloss.
